    "review_notes": [
      "Native source AP735 SPECIAL FUNCTIONS.tif (10200x6600) SHA256 a8896bd1efbe0997e13fe86dc1a1524f1a5c7ba517dafedccb116eb1a42f3fdf. All 30 card faces and 82 physical pin sides, six populated banks, left and right labels, 27 footer references, crossings, and 12 visible diamonds were compared with original-pixel crops. The source TIFF was not modified.",
      "The printed -GROUP 09 CARRY and +CLOCK P2 EXTENDED labels meet on the same source x2195 vertical rail through hollow diamonds; both literal labels are preserved as aliases of one external net. Adjacent no-diamond crossings remain separate.",
      "BG.B13 and BG.D08 form one short isolated local return at source x2275 with no printed active driver. BA.B09 independently feeds AX.D12. The two BG inputs are documented as an undriven isolated jumper; no driver is inferred.",
      "Printed wire qualifiers 2 at AR.B04, AS.B02, AT.B05, AX.D13, AY.D11 and 8 at AZ's second input are separate from physical pin names. Five output ✲ marks are literal print. AK and AM upper left contacts are unlabelled plain inputs; AZ's output is B08 and AT's lower input is D04. The M1 margin reference is DP031AW4 both by the source label and the inline rail, not DP031AWA.",
      "Footer native print controls over A1. Source table readings BC4 02B-E2M7D13, BD4 02B-D1E8A06 and BF4 02A-C1J8E04 were confirmed in tight crops and agree with A1 endpoints. Other A1 differences, including damaged AP735QV4 and omitted connector suffixes, are detailed in FOOTER A1 AUDIT.private.txt; no A1-only characters were inserted into the diagram.",
      "Original scan neighbors: AP731 PROPAGATE SIGN 26-31 PDR ADJ.tif before, AP737 HOT CARRY AND FIXED PT BV.tif after. Source-reviewed owner export awaits separate root hash acceptance."
